  "live_records": {
    "q-59695": {
      "dom_id": "step-q59695",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129811/assets/971ba12add67086eea1d5550efb76688f2b5b33d12dc808146b067a5de088d96.png)\n\nWhat division problem is represented by the model above?",
      "worked_solution": "We have $\\frac{1}{3}$ on the left and $\\frac{1}{9}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129811/assets/fe5aab5aae0d5006aa707732c12e629aa546d83b7ad3204448a5e2f5b0fbfcd8.png)\n\nThe division operation splits the shaded region on the left into $3$ equal parts. So the shaded part on the left is $3$ times larger than the shaded part on the right. \n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷3=\\frac{1}{9}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
