    "q-60996": {
      "dom_id": "step-q60996",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129811/assets/19a6781b69eaa283d5681f6ceb0caae64d7236045796530b4bfb852efb5369ab.png)\n\nWhat division problem is represented by the model above?",
      "worked_solution": "We have $\\frac{1}{6}$ on the left and $\\frac{1}{18}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129811/assets/26b6d4d934870b17480aa5c575c35bdf1603d976982728ab731d887527bd8637.png)\n\nThe division operation splits the shaded region on the left into $3$ equal parts. So the shaded part on the left is $3$ times larger than the shaded part on the right. \n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{6}÷3=\\frac{1}{18}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
